{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks","id":979183,"title":"Indirect Magickal Attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T12:06:25-07:00","id":979183,"title":"Indirect Magickal Attacks","content":"So if I was throwing a fireball I need to roll my Dex + Athletics to try and hit the target.<br /> <br /> What about if I was summoning a piano to fall on someone head. Would there be a \u201cto hit\u201d roll? How would you all play this?<br /> <br /> Or things like shooting fireballs from heaven. Blasting rocks up from the earth.<br /> <br /> If possible, try and stick close to RAW. I do also like to see how people would rule it, so I am looking for both answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:36:32-07:00","id":979203,"title":"","content":"Shooting fireballs from heaven, blasting rocks from below would likely just be AoE attacks. Which are somewhat hard to adjudicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:39:32-07:00","id":979208,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that you wouldn't need to roll to hit when throwing magic at people. The one success to target from the ar\u00eate roll pretty much has that covered.<br /> <br /> Same for the piano, one success to target.<br /> <br /> So long as you can see your target, or have some other connection to them wth Corr, you can target them with one of your ar\u00eate roll's successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T13:32:19-07:00","id":979237,"title":"","content":"Depending on the exact circumstances I would let the target roll Wits+Awareness or something akin. If they score, then they get a chance to dodge. <br /> <br /> A Piano is nothing easy spherewise, I might add:<br /> <br /> Matter 4, Prime 2 to create one and perhaps even Forces to nudge it or grant it a bit more linetic energy.<br /> <br /> Or Entropy 2, Forces 2, Correspondence 2, Matter 2 if there is conveniently one nearby.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3, Matter 3 to use the piano from your sanctum.<br /> <br /> That being said, subtle or difficult to sense attacks work great against sleepers and nightfolk that lacks awareness, auspex, primal urge (etc.)<br /> <br /> Against most awakened foes it is a risk, because they need fewer successes to dodge most of the time.<br /> <br /> Against mages I would rather use enhanced mundane attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:02:55-07:00","id":980594,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to the rules concerning the fireball.<br /> <br /> About the piano, I would not ask for a Dexterity + Athletics of course, but I would require more base successes. At least 3 successes I would say (because letting Pianos fall from the sky is not that easy a task...). Depending on the circonstances, raising the difficulty would be necessary too. If the Mage is using Entropy 2, I would make the dodge roll of the target more difficult, or simply lower the difficulty of the magic roll (not sure how I would take Entropy into account on this one).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:16:11-07:00","id":980597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks#post979183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I was throwing a fireball I need to roll my Dex + Athletics to try and hit the target.<br /> <br /> What about if I was summoning a piano to fall on someone head. Would there be a \u201cto hit\u201d roll? How would you all play this?<br /> <br /> Or things like shooting fireballs from heaven. Blasting rocks up from the earth.<br /> <br /> If possible, try and stick close to RAW. I do also like to see how people would rule it, so I am looking for both answers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Whaaaaaat? Where did you even read that? Who told you that? This is incorrect if you want to follow RAW, unless Storyteller created weird houserules.<br /> <br /> You roll Arete to blast the target, and that's it, unless you're using Violence as Focus. (see below. That's mentioned in magick chart in M20, page 501)<br /> <br /> For dodging, they roll against the amount of your Arete successes. They best it = they evade it. You best them = boom. Magick damage has 2 Health Points per success for a reason, with small dicepool it can be challenging to hit someone, but if you do they're in trouble. Moreover, you can always just attack Pattern with Life or whatever.<br /> <br /> Making things fall on people and everything else is contested with Arete successes vs their dodge successes, at least according to M20.<br /> <br /> Now if you want Environmental Damage, there's a whole section about that in M20 (making things fall on people, smashing them into walls, ramming them, making them fall from high places and more).<br /> <br /> <br /> But, while we're at it, about rolling for mundane attack AND Arete at same turn. That's called using VIolence as Focus.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> John Courage is about to fight some vampire in the alley. He uses his Entropy 4 in order to deliver a bone-crushing strike right to vampire's face, and scores 3 successes. That's 6 levels of Damage.<br /> <br /> Now, he rolls his 4 Dexterity and 4 Brawl to hit the said vampire (he rolls both mundane attack and Arete roll separately, but in the same turn). He scores 4 successes, and unless the vampire can dodge that, the hit connects.<br /> <br /> That's where you roll your mundane Abillities to hit the target, as per chart on page 501. If it's purely magickal attack (throwing fireball), you only roll Arete.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:03:53-07:00","id":980617,"title":"","content":"And the etherite fireball throwing gun shaped object?<br /> <br /> Seriously, I do not get the difference between a Bone Crushing Strike and a Fiery Orb.<br /> Naturally, you can design a Forces effect to engulf the target in flames, and there you need not roll to hit.<br /> But your view of it means that there never will be a stray fireball, because a fireball that does not hit has zero damage and no intelligent mage would ever use \u201cpurely\u201c magickal attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:13:51-07:00","id":980647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980617#post980617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the etherite fireball throwing gun shaped object?<br /> <br /> Seriously, I do not get the difference between a Bone Crushing Strike and a Fiery Orb.<br /> Naturally, you can design a Forces effect to engulf the target in flames, and there you need not roll to hit.<br /> But your view of it means that there never will be a stray fireball, because a fireball that does not hit has zero damage and no intelligent mage would ever use \u201cpurely\u201c magickal attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Pulls Paradigms card*<br /> <br /> As you just said, instead of throwing said fireball, you can engulf the target in flames, but both count as pure magickal attacks. Violence as Focus is described as &quot;magickally enhanced mundane attack&quot; (example: the said bone-crushing strike).<br /> <br /> OP said he wants RAW and I gave him that.<br /> <br /> And well, yeah, I guess that's exactly what M20 implies. Magickal attack and throwing fireballs is like.. the more Enlightened you are, the more precise you are and you get more successes and it's harder to dodge?<br /> <br /> Though, I suppose that's why NWO agents do not rely on magick (unlike some Tradition mages do), and instead they hone their mundane combat skills in order to land the magickal attack. It does make sense to call in for &quot;special training&quot; when it comes to using Violence as Focus, because I personally do not expect a random mage to just start using it out of nowhere. He'd need to at least, I don't know, practice how to do that or at least guess it's a thing, or something like that? If not, that just makes NWO lengthy training not so worth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:41:14-07:00","id":980658,"title":"","content":"Ok, lets say you use Forces 3 Prime 3 to charge a pebble (make a charm). If you later use it you need no roll to hit, the magick is doing that for you. And luckily you spend some time and managed to get 10 successes for damage. Now it is highly unlikely to dodge this pebble of fiery doom. Even if you dodge with 6 successes you take 8 levels of agg.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:52:05-07:00","id":980662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980658#post980658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, lets say you use Forces 3 Prime 3 to charge a pebble (make a charm). If you later use it you need no roll to hit, the magick is doing that for you. And luckily you spend some time and managed to get 10 successes for damage. Now it is highly unlikely to dodge this pebble of fiery doom. Even if you dodge with 6 successes you take 8 levels of agg.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Use it how, exactly?<br /> <br /> If you throw that pebble, throwing = mundane attack. Gotta roll that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:58:51-07:00","id":980663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980662#post980662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Use it how, exactly?<br /> <br /> If you throw that pebble, throwing = mundane attack. Gotta roll that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Throwing something is a mundane attack.<br /> A Fireball is something.<br /> <br /> Conclusio:<br /> Throwing a fireball is a mundane attack.<br /> Gotta roll that.<br /> <br /> q.e.d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:13:00-07:00","id":980667,"title":"","content":"Havent read M20 but in every other edition an Indirect Magical Attack relies on an Attack and Ar\u00eate roll (shooting the plasma rifle, firing the ray gun, tossing the lightning bolt, hurling the knife of endings etc) which can be dodged like any other attack and also functions like any other attack. This also tends not to require a Pattern Sphere to effect the target. A Direct Magical Attack effects a Pattern Direct (hence the name) turning motion into heat (curse of friction rote) or flesh into fire or shattering bones with a curse requires no attack roll or allows for a dodge roll, exceptions are Mind Magics which give a defensive WP roll but only if the subject is aware they are under mental attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:19:34-07:00","id":980668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980663#post980663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Throwing something is a mundane attack.<br /> A Fireball is something.<br /> <br /> Conclusio:<br /> Throwing a fireball is a mundane attack.<br /> Gotta roll that.<br /> <br /> q.e.d.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That now is how you put it. Pebble is mundane item, and you're not going to get Paradox for throwing that pebble (unless it explodes or does something outrageously vulgar).<br /> <br /> Fireball isn't that, and is pretty much a magickal attack. To each their own though, just like many other thigns in Mage you can look at it under different points of view.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:21:07-07:00","id":980684,"title":"","content":"I am sorry, but that is how RAW puts it as well. (Emphasis mine)<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 p.536</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Magickal Attack Rolls</b><br /> <br /> Under many circumstances, you simply roll your character\u2019s Arete, plus or minus modifiers, to see whether an Effect goes off. If you succeed, then the Effect succeeds as well. In certain circumstances, though, you need to<b> hit a target who doesn\u2019t want to be hit</b>. Perhaps you\u2019re firing an energy gun, swinging an enchanted sword, or <b>flinging the archetypal fireball</b> at your intended target of misfortune. <b>In such situations, you also need to roll an attack to hit that person</b>. The Effect might succeed, but its impact may go elsewhere.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:19:41-07:00","id":980728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980684#post980684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sorry, but that is how RAW puts it as well. (Emphasis mine)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Odd. I've seen pure magickal attacks being ruled the other way around.<br /> <br /> Now that begs for a question why would one want to throw a fireball if they can just set someone on fire without having to roll for hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:46:00-07:00","id":980741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980728#post980728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Odd. I've seen pure magickal attacks being ruled the other way around.<br /> <br /> Now that begs for a question why would one want to throw a fireball if they can just set someone on fire without having to roll for hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, doesn't immolating someone directly require Life for targeting purposes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:28:02-07:00","id":980765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980728#post980728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Odd. I've seen pure magickal attacks being ruled the other way around.<br /> <br /> Now that begs for a question why would one want to throw a fireball if they can just set someone on fire without having to roll for hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting character example:<br /> Arete 3 Forces3 Life3 Prime2 Dex+Ath 5<br /> <br /> Fireball (Arete against TN 7) we generously assume he gets the 3 successes needed for a fireball (m20 p. 503). The target (dex+ath 4) rolls for dodge and scores 2 successes.<br /> That means the target gets burned for 4 levels of agg (bonus success from forces).<br /> <br /> Now assume you need to roll to hit (all else being equal).<br /> The mage scores 3 successes to hit with his 5 dice.<br /> Subtract 2 for dodge, the fireball still hits.<br /> 3(+1 for Forces) means 8 levels of agg.<br /> <br /> As long as you have more dices in the suitable attribute+ability than in Arete, you are better off rolling to hit.<br /> <br /> Pattern Attacks are a different story.<br /> <br /> Rip the man body with the above 3 successes are 6 levels agg. Only Countermagic can help in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T07:58:22-07:00","id":980770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=980728#post980728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Odd. I've seen pure magickal attacks being ruled the other way around.<br /> <br /> Now that begs for a question why would one want to throw a fireball if they can just set someone on fire without having to roll for hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This question has been asked several times and I would answer the same way as before. May be because you do not know how to do it an other way. This thing is very paradigm dependent.<br /> <br /> I agree you would ask why someone casts a fireball if they just can ignite the target in one second. However, not all Mages can cast fire from nothing and shape them into a tower of flames around a target. Depending on your paradigm, it may not be even possible. These rules are general guidelines so of course, if the Mage know how to directly attack someone's pattern, casting a fireball is not adviced. But if he can not, he would have to adapt. Exemple : throwing existing flames at someone because you do not know Prime and can not create them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:53:53-07:00","id":982794,"title":"","content":"Sorry for making a post then having life jump me in a dark ally and bend a trashcan around me (ok, maybe I have had a little time to catch a couple episodes of Luke Cage).<br /> <br /> I see this conversation has spun into a tangent and I see most questions have been answered.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Concerning</i></b>: <i>Why would anyone make an effect that forces the player to have to roll to hit vs just rolling the magic (ie, bursting flames where a person is standing vs hitting them with a fireball. Or using a thousand other things people can think of using forces).</i><br /> <br /> I assume most mage players are reasonably intelligent people and they can figure out how to create a \u201c<i>curse effect\u201d</i> vs a \u201c<i>physical effect\u201d </i><i>(lack of better words)</i> while staying inside of the characters paradigm.<br /> <br /> The above is a problem I am having with the game and part of the reason that spur this conversation. If I do Rip the Man Body, the only \u201cdodge\u201d the target has is with countermagick. Which is cool. I can deal with that and it makes sense. If I throw a magick something at the target, they can try and dodge out of the way. I think this is a cool idea and it also makes sense. But where is the mechanical benefit? I mean this is a game, if there is a yang then there should be a ying. Why would I give the target a dodge roll, when if I think for 5 more seconds, I can take away their dodge roll?<br /> <br /> My group has been trying to use the rules for Violence Enhances Magick for all physical attacks. So if Attacker rolls 5 successes and defender rolls 3 successes the effect has -2 difficulty to be that much better. It was a little TOO good, so we make one minor adjustment. We treat it like an attack roll. The first success is a hit, the second success reduces the difficulty. It has worked so far for us, but we have only been trying it out for a few get togethers.<br /> <br /> I notice people in the game now make a decision based on what makes a better scene vs what is more efficient. Mostly because we all agree that between these two attacks they are sorta balanced now. One way gets a dodge and a possible reduced difficulty and the other way rolls effect vs counter magick. There are benefits on both sides.<br /> <br /> Whereas before my players were like, \u201cWell X seems like something my character would do, but she could also do Y and Y has a better chance of success right now so I am doing Y.\u201d<br /> <br /> The only other suggestion I received was give the attacker an additional damage dice to be tacked on to the effect. But that means one attack could have a total of 4 rolls. (Attack, dodge, ar\u00eate, and bonus dice). I already feel we roll a lot\u2026 well in combat that is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Which leads me back to my original post:</b><br /> Then we ran into this question. \u201cWhat if I want to flip a car on someone or pull a bank safe out of the sky? What do I roll for attack?\u201d This look like something from page 417 (openly magickal or Indirect assault) where it says you roll your Arete as your attack roll. That doesn\u2019t make ANY sense to me. We used our characters to test this. I made my Arete roll and the other player rolled their Dex+Athletics to dodge. Then we tried this with mooks. We have starting characters Arete 3 (a schooled mage), but Dex+Athletics using a mook thug from the back of the book starts with 4 dice. You could probably tell, we were not hitting much.<br /> <br /> So that is when I reached out to you all. Maybe someone will say something that makes sense.<br /> <br /> What would be a good attack roll for someone making something fall out of the sky, flipping a car onto a target, making a rock fly out of the ground to hit someone, doing a gesture with their hand and a fireball flies out of the clouds?<br /> <br /> If there isn\u2019t an attack roll, the target should get a chance to dodge, what do they roll against? Do I create a random successes needed? What kind of mechanic would work well here? Is there something already and I am missing it?<br /> <br /> All help is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:48:06-07:00","id":982865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982794#post982794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for making a post then having life jump me in a dark ally and bend a trashcan around me (ok, maybe I have had a little time to catch a couple episodes of Luke Cage).<br /> But where is the mechanical benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are none and there should not be. You have the possibility to do it. If you do not want to, then don't. But you can, that's all. It's like saying that there's no mechanical benefit to take the time to go to the library if you can have access to the internet. If you prefer to go to the library, then go, if you prefer google, then don't go to the library. No need to wonder if one is more efficient than the other. The possibility just exist and you should have the choice in your actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982794#post982794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice people in the game now make a decision based on what makes a better scene vs what is more efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my sessions, they do that because we're playing Mage in a narrative way, so the choice of a better scene will always prevail on the most efficient action. Because poeple do not always act with logic in real life. And because it's fun to cast a fireball.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982794#post982794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Which leads me back to my original post:</b><br /> Then we ran into this question. \u201cWhat if I want to flip a car on someone or pull a bank safe out of the sky? What do I roll for attack?\u201d This look like something from page 417 (openly magickal or Indirect assault) where it says you roll your Arete as your attack roll. That doesn\u2019t make ANY sense to me. We used our characters to test this. I made my Arete roll and the other player rolled their Dex+Athletics to dodge. Then we tried this with mooks. We have starting characters Arete 3 (a schooled mage), but Dex+Athletics using a mook thug from the back of the book starts with 4 dice. You could probably tell, we were not hitting much.<br /> <br /> So that is when I reached out to you all. Maybe someone will say something that makes sense.<br /> <br /> What would be a good attack roll for someone making something fall out of the sky, flipping a car onto a target, making a rock fly out of the ground to hit someone, doing a gesture with their hand and a fireball flies out of the clouds?<br /> <br /> If there isn\u2019t an attack roll, the target should get a chance to dodge, what do they roll against? Do I create a random successes needed? What kind of mechanic would work well here? Is there something already and I am missing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, you did it right. If you let a bank safe fall from the sky and the target has 4 die in Dex+Ath and you have only 3 in Arete, then yes, he has better chance, but you get to choose the difficulty of his roll. Exemple : If the safe appears ten meters above the target, he has time to see it and dodge it. If it appears 1 cm above him... well... I think he should not even have the right to roll. Nobody can dodge that with a mundane roll. So as always, it depends on the way the scene is described because before all things, Mage is a narrative game (at least in my opinion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 10-06-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:45:10-07:00","id":982904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982865#post982865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are none and there should not be. It's like saying that there's no mechanical benefit to take the time to go to the library if you can have access to the internet. If you prefer to go to the library, then go, if you prefer google, then don't go to the library.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is absolutely a mechanical benefit of going to the library. You have librarians, who will help you dig up research. The yin is that it is just slower. The yang is that with the additional resources you could get better research.<br /> <br /> But we digress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982865#post982865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my sessions, they do that because we're playing Mage in a narrative way, so the choice of a better scene will always prevail on the most efficient action. Because poeple do not always act with logic in real life. And because it's fun to cast a fireball.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes yes... people should do it because it is playing their characters. I get that, but sometimes when your character is in a &quot;immabout to die&quot; situation, you are going to do whatever you need to do to live. Since this is a game it sounds like more fun if the players have options for their characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982865#post982865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, you did it right. If you let a bank safe fall from the sky and the target has 4 die in Dex+Ath and you have only 3 in Arete, then yes, he has better chance, but you get to choose the difficulty of his roll. Exemple : If the safe appears ten meters above the target, he has time to see it and dodge it. If it appears 1 cm above him... well... I think he should not even have the right to roll. Nobody can dodge that with a mundane roll. So as always, it depends on the way the scene is described because before all things, Mage is a narrative game (at least in my opinion).</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have done the right thing ruleswise, but sure as heck felt broken. One of my players said it best. I may as well give up magick and just shoot the guy. I have a better chance to do something mundanely then I do with phenomenal cosmic power minus the itty bitty living space.<br /> <br /> He was kind of right (albeit being a little hyperbolic) about this. He may as well summon fire around a guy the whole night instead of stepping outside of his efficiency zone and do something cool like flip a car on someone.<br /> <br /> I feel there should be some kind of better way to handle attacking with magick then rolling Arete (which is super costly to lift and can only start at 3) and letting the defender roll Dex+Athletics (easily capable of starting with 6 dice).<br /> <br /> So yes, the <b><i>inexperience mook</i></b> had a better dice pool than the <b><i>Schooled Mage</i></b>. It would be just like <i>IF</i> the mechanic for shooting a gun was changed to <i>Firearms</i> vs <i>Dex + Athletics</i>.<br /> <br /> Even the 3<sup>rd</sup> ed storyteller book touched on how unbalanced this was and offered up a suggestion of rolling Arete + Sphere for the attack, but said this can get off balance in the other direction with experienced characters. I was a little surprised this mechanic wasn\u2019t touched in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:49:35-07:00","id":982941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982904#post982904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is absolutely a mechanical benefit of going to the library. You have librarians, who will help you dig up research. The yin is that it is just slower. The yang is that with the additional resources you could get better research.<br /> <br /> But we digress.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it seems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982904#post982904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes yes... people should do it because it is playing their characters. I get that, but sometimes when your character is in a &quot;immabout to die&quot; situation, you are going to do whatever you need to do to live. Since this is a game it sounds like more fun if the players have options for their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the case. You can do pretty much everything, even inefficient ones. Your &quot;yes, yes&quot; sounds like you're tired of poeple recalling you that RPG is about playing a role... :'(<br /> <br /> And even in complex situations, poeple (even Mages) make mistakes or die. I had a player once that decided to let his character die because he could not see a way out when considering the personnality of his character. He was nor sad nor mad. He just stated that there was no way out of his situation. He made another one.<br /> <br /> As another exemple, I had a character that went so far into darkness that he became one of the villain of my campaign and his player had to make another character, the first one becoming a NPC. RPG means Role-Playing-Game and in my opinion, that can not be put aside. I would go even further, I will play no rule that will diminish that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=982904#post982904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have done the right thing ruleswise, but sure as heck felt broken. One of my players said it best. I may as well give up magick and just shoot the guy. I have a better chance to do something mundanely then I do with phenomenal cosmic power minus the itty bitty living space.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is absolutely true and I see nothing wront in that. Not all situation can be solved with magick nor should be. In any case, a gun is often more efficient than a ligthning strike and I cannot see the problem of that.<br /> <br /> Did you ever try to create a villain that was a Sleeper with no connection to the supernatural in any form ? Such like that good Awful Corupted Politician kind of guy ? It is very interesting because in those scenarii, most of the time, no magick is involved. The Ascension War is also a fight in open space against standard sleeper auto-destructive behavior. That's not because you're a Mage that magick is only solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:01:20-07:00","id":983010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your &quot;yes, yes&quot; sounds like you're tired of people recalling you that RPG is about playing a role... :'( </div> </div> </div>That is not what I mean by &quot;Yes Yes&quot;. Every time I try to have a conversation about mechanics someone jumps out and wants to talk about the role part. RP isn't a problem. You can role play with any game. My friends and I dress up and RP our characters when we play board games. We do this often with zombiecide. I have played many Table Top board games and RPGs. I have attended a few different LARPS. RolePlay is pretty consistent across all these types of games. The difference between all of these games are mechanics.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, RP enhances a game, but the mechanics are what make and break games. \u201cWhat allows the player to best be the character they designed without rules?\u201d That is the question I rate every TTRPG on. Obviously the character must be created within the theme of the game (ie a player wants to play a vampire in Star Wars, most SW TTRPGs are not designed for that). This is one reason why FATE is my favorite TTRPG.<br /> <br /> <br /> So when I ask about these things, I am focusing on mechanics. If I want to build a mage that throws things around like a car, fridge, rocks from the ground. Mechanic wise I am at a disadvantage to someone who does the exact same thing, but with a gun, with their throwing arm, with a sling shot and more. <br /> <br /> This, to me, is a problem with the system. A player should be able to play any kind of mage character they want and we should be able to look at the system on a fundamental level and say &quot;You are doing a (sphere) effect. It is a physical attack; the target gets to dodge; effect is determined by Ar\u00eate roll.&quot; <br /> <br /> Non-dodge-able (curse) type actions all work like this. Doesn\u2019t matter if you have to make soup, dance, throw a hissy fit, speak Latin, or poop to cast your spell. You roll Arete; target rolls counter magick; effect is determined by Ar\u00eate.<br /> <br /> So, if they are throwing a fireball, punching, tossing a car, spitting, or some dodge-able action. These should all fundamentally work the same. Roll some kind of Attribute+Skill combo to attack, Target rolls Attribute+Skill combo to defend and on hit effect is determined by Arete roll.<br /> <br /> This is how I feel it should work. I am just trying to get there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:17:04-07:00","id":983174,"title":"","content":"I handle a fireball like any other attack, but to cut on the dierolls it gets one additional level of damage per 2 successes above 1.<br /> <br /> Regarding the matter of things falling from the sky:<br /> Do not forget that to dodge something you have to sense it first. And most falling things are not that loud. As I posted earlier this is a great attack against mooks. They don't sense it, because they lack awareness and don't look up often.<br /> <br /> If you need a to hit roll, I would recommend Wits+Alertness (Tetris being a fitting speciality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:21:30-07:00","id":983244,"title":"","content":"For risk of repeating... If you are making an attack roll for the fireball etc then you are adding extra successes to damage. This can make it more effective than targeting the pattern direct as if successful you getting to add to the base damage of the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T04:28:16-07:00","id":983247,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2767_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2767\" data-vbnamecard=\"2767\">Moirdryd</a> that was another reason we decided not to tack on bonus damage. The primary reason was just too much rolling. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12022_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12022\" data-vbnamecard=\"12022\">Nonsense</a> what would be a good rule of thumb if they do pass their aleadtness roll for their dodge roll?<br /> <br /> Also what about throwing a car at them, or flinging something off the ground?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2900,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","user":"frostbyte000jm","date":". 10-07-2016, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:57:21-07:00","id":983270,"title":"","content":"Why would you need anything more than matter 3 for the Piano? It seems like the progression in my mind of stupid stuff to drop on someone is: matter 2 for a single fairly homogeneous object, so in this example an anvil. Matter 3 would be a more complex object made of mutiple things would be matter 3, and matter 5 if you wanted to drop a small nuclear reactor on someone(because plutonium is exotic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T06:56:11-07:00","id":983290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=983270#post983270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you need anything more than matter 3 for the Piano?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the piano coming from? If the piano was already suspended in the air, sure Matter could make the ropes break. But if the Piano didn't exist you need to create it, so you need Prime 2 + Matter 3/4 a Piano could be pretty complex. If the piano existed in a nearby hotel you could use correspondence 3 + matter 3 to pull it through without touching it. <br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t really want to focus on the spheres for this conversation tho. There are many other pages that get into those debates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:24:09-07:00","id":983298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=983247#post983247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> that was another reason we decided not to tack on bonus damage. The primary reason was just too much rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of that I convert 2 successes into 1 LEVEL of damage instead of 1 success into 1 DIE of damage. It works IMHO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/979183-indirect-magickal-attacks?p=983247#post983247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> what would be a good rule of thumb if they do pass their aleadtness roll for their dodge roll?<br /> <br /> Also what about throwing a car at them, or flinging something off the ground?</div> </div> </div> </div>At my table mooks don't get a alertness roll in this kind of situations. They are just mooks after all, not worth so much attention to make needless rolls.<br /> <br /> That being said my 2 cents:<br /> If the target of your falling piano has awareness I would say TN 5-7, if not TN 6-8 (depends a lot on exact circumstances).<br /> <br /> Flinging things from groundlevel at a target could be Strenght+Do, Manipulation+Intimidate, Perception+Esoterics, Intelligence+Physics, etc.<br /> It depends on the mage in question (and his way of doing magick).<br /> <br /> And if a car behind the target gets flung on a mook how should he know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:22:54-07:00","id":983332,"title":"","content":"On the topic of this...<br /> <br /> Let's say I use a taser to shoot someone while also delivering...say Life 3 and maybe Forces to overload their brain essentially and deal agg damage (I believe &quot;how do you do that&quot; says that life 3 can deal agg in certain circumstances). Does the taser also do its normal effect in addition to the magic damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:52:50-07:00","id":983350,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2818_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2818\" data-vbnamecard=\"2818\">FrostFox</a>, Some people house rule that it does, but RAW says it doesn't... can someone help me out and find a page number? I am failing today (lack of sleep).<br /> <br /> Nevermind! I found it. [M20: p413] &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If a weapon is being used as a focus instrument, then the damage from that magickal Effect reflects the damage of that weapon.&quot;</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2900,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","user":"frostbyte000jm","date":".  Edit: because I found it. 10-07-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:34:54-07:00","id":983368,"title":"","content":"Basically you have several choices:<br /> <br /> 1. The taser is the focus of the Rip the man body effect. Arete successes determine damage, the to hit roll lowers TN.<br /> <br /> 2. Your effect enhances your mundane attack. Arete successes lower TN of the to hit roll.<br /> <br /> 3. Your effect increases the damage the taser does. you upgrade it to lethal/agg and/or you add 1 level of damage per Arete success.<br /> <br /> All of this options should be usable even if the taser is fired by someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:43:10-07:00","id":983373,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12022_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12022\" data-vbnamecard=\"12022\">Nonsense</a> ... I give up... what does TN mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:50:26-07:00","id":983379,"title":"","content":"Target Number. Sorry I thought it was an established shorthand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:01:46-07:00","id":983386,"title":"","content":"It probably is, I was just not used to it. Thanx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}